%% Sequence Diagram: Youth Account Management API - Parent Fund Allocation
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Parent as Parent/Guardian
  participant WebApp as Banking Web Application
  participant API as Youth Account Management Service
  participant AccountSvc as Account Service
  participant PaymentSvc as Payment Service
  participant TransSvc as Transaction Service
  note over Parent,API: All API calls require OAuth2, RBAC, and are audit-logged.
  Parent->>WebApp: Login (OAuth2)
  WebApp->>API: GET /api/youth-accounts/{id}/dashboard (OAuth2 token)
  API->>AccountSvc: Fetch account details
  API->>TransSvc: Fetch recent transactions
  API-->>WebApp: Dashboard (account, limits, transactions)
  WebApp-->>Parent: Display dashboard
  Parent->>WebApp: Initiate fund transfer
  WebApp->>API: POST /api/youth-accounts/{id}/fund-transfer (body, OAuth2 token)
  API->>PaymentSvc: Initiate fund transfer
  API->>AccountSvc: Update balance
  API-->>WebApp: Transfer result (status, updated balance)
  WebApp-->>Parent: Show transfer result
  Parent->>WebApp: Set spending limit
  WebApp->>API: PUT /api/youth-accounts/{id}/spending-limit (body, OAuth2 token)
  API->>API: Update spending limit in DB
  API-->>WebApp: Limit update result
  WebApp-->>Parent: Show limit update status
  Parent->>WebApp: View transactions
  WebApp->>API: GET /api/youth-accounts/{id}/transactions (params, OAuth2 token)
  API->>TransSvc: Fetch transactions
  API-->>WebApp: Transaction list
  WebApp-->>Parent: Show transaction history
  note over API: All actions are RBAC-enforced and audit-logged (per NFR).